--TEST--
`Core\Markdown::fromHtml` collapses whitespace, unwraps a `div`, escapes a number at the start of a line and inline syntax characters, writes a `javascript:` link as its text, percent-encodes a URL, and cuts a web address so it does not become a link — `rule:core-classes/markdown-from-html`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Markdown::fromHtml
// Spaces, tabs and line breaks in text collapse to one space.
echo Core\Markdown::fromHtml("<div>\n  <p>  many    spaces\n\tand a tab  </p>\n</div>");
echo "--\n";
// A number and a dot at the start of a line get a backslash, so the line is not a list.
echo Core\Markdown::fromHtml("<p>1. not a list</p><p>a_b and [x] and `y`</p>");
echo "--\n";
// A `javascript:` link is written as its text alone.
echo Core\Markdown::fromHtml("<p><a href=\"javascript:alert(1)\">click</a> and <a href=\"/Straße\">street</a></p>");
echo "--\n";
// Text that looks like a web address is cut with an empty comment, so it is not a link.
echo Core\Markdown::fromHtml("<p>visit www.example.com today</p>");
--EXPECT--
many spaces and a tab
--
1\. not a list

a\_b and \[x\] and \`y\`
--
click and [street](/Stra%C3%9Fe)
--
visit www<!-- -->.example.com today
